---
import PersonalVault from "@/layouts/PersonalVault.astro";
import { withBase } from "@/utils/path";
---

<PersonalVault
	title="Terms of use"
	description="Purpose, authorized use, and limitations of Henrique Bastos's private Personal Vault application."
>
	<h1>Terms of use</h1>
	<p>
		Personal Vault is a private application operated by Henrique Bastos. It is not a public
		subscription service and does not offer public account registration.
	</p>

	<h2>1 Authorized use</h2>
	<p>
		I use Personal Vault only with accounts and documents I am authorized to access. Access through
		Google OAuth does not replace meeting consent, confidentiality duties, or an organization's data
		policies.
	</p>
	<p>
		I am responsible for having permission to save meeting content and send selected content to
		storage or AI providers.
	</p>

	<h2>2 Access and availability</h2>
	<p>
		Google account permissions and organization policies control access to source information.
		Personal Vault does not bypass those controls.
	</p>
	<p>
		The application may change, stop working, or become unavailable. Google APIs and other providers
		can change their features, limits, and requirements.
	</p>

	<h2>3 Accuracy</h2>
	<p>
		Meeting notes, transcripts, and AI-generated summaries can be incomplete or incorrect. I check
		important details against their sources before relying on them.
	</p>
	<p>
		A summary or storyboard does not replace a complete transcript, and a transcript does not
		necessarily capture the entire meeting.
	</p>

	<h2>4 Data and ownership</h2>
	<p>
		Importing information does not transfer ownership of the source material. The <a
			href={withBase("/apps/personal-vault/privacy/")}>privacy policy</a
		> explains how data is accessed, stored, processed, and removed.
	</p>

	<h2>5 Independent application</h2>
	<p>
		Personal Vault is not a Google product and is not endorsed by Google. Google, Obsidian, and any
		AI or storage providers remain subject to their own terms.
	</p>

	<h2>6 Contact and changes</h2>
	<p>
		Questions about the application or these terms can be sent to <a
			href="mailto:henrique@bastos.net">henrique@bastos.net</a
		>. I may revise these terms as the application changes.
	</p>
</PersonalVault>
